seg: opencv-python-headless and a pinned project build backend. Apply from the
repository root with deploy/patches/apply-pyproject-patches.sh (git apply, then `uv lock`; only the
opencv entries and a [manifest] table change in uv.lock: opencv-python goes, opencv-python-headless
comes). The hunks carry one line of context, not three, so that an edit next to them (the text of the
`slow` marker moved the context once, and the patch stopped applying) does not break them.

opencv: opencv-python's cv2 needs libGL.so.1, libglib2.0-0, libgthread, libX11 and libxcb at import
time (checked with ldd on the locked wheel); the headless wheel of the same version needs only libc, libm,
libgcc_s and libstdc++ (checked the same way). With it the runtime image has no apt packages at all,
no X11 or mesa libraries to patch, and the wheel is 13 MB smaller. The service never opens a window.
Both wheels provide the module cv2, so installing both would clash: the direct dependency becomes the
headless wheel at the locked version (4.11.0.86) and [tool.uv] exclude-dependencies removes
opencv-python from the resolution altogether (it is not in uv.lock). The first version of this patch used
an override with a marker that never matches (the trick services/cls uses for ipyplot); that leaves an
sdist-only opencv-python entry in the lock, and the next `uv lock` after any manifest change (a pin, a new
dependency) failed with "Failed to download and build opencv-python==4.11.0.86". exclude-dependencies has
no such entry: a re-lock after a changed pin works (checked in a scratch copy).
decimer-segmentation 1.6.0 (the release; before it, git commit 6914cac) still declares opencv-python, so
the exclusion is still needed.
Without this patch, build the image with --build-arg OPENCV_GUI_LIBS=1 instead.

build pin: `uv sync --no-editable` builds the project and its path dependency (services/common) from
source during the install, in an isolated build environment whose backend uv resolves fresh from PyPI.
That code runs at install time with network access, so an unpinned backend makes the image
non-reproducible, although uv.lock pins every runtime package. [tool.uv] build-constraint-dependencies
pins uv-build, the projects' own backend, to the version CI uses (0.13.5). uv.lock records the
constraints in its [manifest], so `uv sync --locked` needs the lock refreshed after the patch:
apply-pyproject-patches.sh does it. Until the P2-02b re-pin this list also pinned setuptools 84.0.0 for
the git build of decimer-segmentation (a setup.py project, built from source at install time); 1.6.0 is
a wheel from PyPI, so no third-party backend runs for seg any more and that pin is gone. cls and chem
still have git dependencies and still pin theirs (cls-pyproject.patch, chem-pyproject.patch).

--- a/services/seg/pyproject.toml
+++ b/services/seg/pyproject.toml
@@ -13,3 +13,3 @@
     "numpy==1.26.3",
-    "opencv-python>=4.11.0.86",
+    "opencv-python-headless==4.11.0.86",
     "protobuf==4.25.1",
@@ -48,2 +48,19 @@
 ]
+
+[tool.uv]
+# The service imports cv2 but never opens a window. opencv-python also needs libGL.so.1 and
+# libglib2.0-0 at import time; the headless wheel does not, so the runtime image needs no apt
+# packages. decimer-segmentation declares opencv-python, so it is excluded from the resolution
+# (not locked at all), and the headless wheel, pinned to the version that was locked before (the
+# two wheels share a version scheme), is a direct dependency instead. Not an override with a marker
+# that never matches: that leaves an sdist-only opencv-python entry in uv.lock, which every later
+# `uv lock` has to build to read its metadata.
+exclude-dependencies = ["opencv-python"]
+# The project's own build backend is pinned too (deploy/patches): `uv sync --no-editable` builds
+# decimer-seg and decimer-service from source in an isolated environment, and without this uv takes
+# the newest uv-build that [build-system] allows. CI uses 0.13.5. decimer-segmentation itself is a
+# wheel from PyPI (1.6.0), so no third-party build backend runs at install time.
+build-constraint-dependencies = [
+    "uv-build==0.13.5",
+]
 
